messages:
nina: Heads-up, Saturn Health POC starting next week. They want a focused doc showing: ephemeral handshake, streaming settings to avoid backpressure, how tool/function calls are surfaced, and how we validate structured JSON output. Can we make a tiny copy-paste cheat-sheet? :memo:
omar: Hosted for the POC? If so we should include retry/backoff guidance for transient 429s.
nina: Yes hosted. Keep it minimal, theyre non-technical clinicians but our contact dev will run the integration.
lucy: Quick checklist I usually give presales: 1) get ephemeral token from presales API 2) wire token into SDK credentialProvider 3) open stream with `rwd-stream-v1` subprotocol 4) send meta/schema frame 5) listen for `toolcall` events and reply with `tool_response` frames 6) enable `strict_schema_validation` if they want strong regression alerts.
omar: For streaming knobs: recommend `max_inflight=8`, `window_ms=200`, and `heartbeat=15s`. That keeps latency low and prevents runaway concurrency on client side. If they need higher throughput, use short batch REST calls with `concurrency=16` server-side.
lucy: Example WebSocket handshake (curl to get ephemeral token):
```bash
curl -sS -X POST "https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer PRESALES_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"account":"saturn-health","purpose":"poc"}'
# returns {"token":"ey...","expires_in":900}
```
nina: And minimal client flow (Node sample):
```js
// credential provider auto-refresh
const client = new RedwoodClient({
  credentialProvider: async () => ({ token: await getEphemeral() }),
  streaming: true
});

const ws = await client.openStream({ model: 'rwd-4-small', multiplex: true });
// send schema up-front
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'meta', schema_id: 'saturn-v1', strict: true }));

ws.on('message', async (msg) => {
  if (msg.type === 'toolcall') {
    const result = await callExternalApi(msg.payload);
    ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'tool_response', id: msg.id, result }));
  }
  if (msg.type === 'chunk') { /* aggregate tokens */ }
});
```
omar: For structured output validation: include a JSON Schema and set `strict: true` in meta. SDK will emit `schema_violation` events which you can route to alerts/eval harness. Recommend a small set of golden prompts so we can track regressions.
lucy: Pricing note for presales: 40 req/s @ ~1k tokens/resp => ~40k tokens/sec => ~3.5B tokens/day if run 24/7. That's large for hosted — for a business-hours POC the daily tokens are much lower. Ballpark advice: run a 1-2 hour test with representative inputs to measure real token usage, then we can estimate cost and suggest a short Dedicated trial if needed. I'll DM finance for a quick ballpark figure we can share.
nina: Can you drop a one-paragraph plug-and-play runbook I can paste into the customer onboarding doc? Short, copyable.
lucy: Pasteable runbook (single-paragraph + curl):
"1) Request an ephemeral token from our presales endpoint using your account id. 2) Use the token with the Redwood SDK's credentialProvider to open a streaming connection (subprotocol `rwd-stream-v1`), send a `meta` frame with `schema_id` and optional `strict` flag, then stream inputs. 3) Handle `toolcall` messages from the runtime and reply with `tool_response` frames; for bulk work use short batch REST endpoints. 4) If throughput exceeds hosted quotas, request a short Dedicated trial. Example handshake curl: `curl -X POST https://presales.redwood.ai/v1/ephemeral -H 'Authorization: Bearer PRESALES_KEY' -d '{"account":"saturn-health"}'`"
omar: I'll attach a tiny demo repo and ping finance with the quick pricing ballpark.
infra-bot: presales/demo-repo v0.9 deployed to presales-bucket (files: runbook.md, node-examples.js) :white_check_mark:
nina: Perfect, thanks everyone. I'll send this to the customer and include the demo link. If they ask about SOC2/KMS we can loop security but not yet.
